a rescue team throws a lifeline to abdul  majid's family his daughter-in-law is  eight months pregnant and needs urgent  medical care they had been stranded for  days when they spotted this rescue boat  and called for help  we faced a lot of difficulty for four  days it was tough to get food and  drinking water we eventually got some  relief the water level was about one and  a half meters high  heavy rains have caused floods in parts  of assam state in india's northeast  impacting 700 000 people  hojai district in central assam is one  of the worst affected areas  thousands of homes have been damaged  since flooding began last week  receding water levels are making it more  difficult to evacuate people  rescue boats like this one continue to  cross over submerged paddy fields the  water in some parts is estimated to be  at least 15 feet deep the retrieving  bodies carrying relief material and  rescuing stranded villagers who've been  stuck without food and other necessities  for days  dozens of families are staying in this  relief camp some have been staying for a  week they say they need more help from  the government  we worry about our future we don't know  what we will do we don't think there's  any hope for us we have left our cattle  and we don't have enough to eat we have  been here for a while and we are still  waiting for help  assam often sees floods during the  monsoon season this year the rains have  come early and are more intense hojai  hasn't seen major flooding in 18 years  our main challenge was the communication  how we reached to the people so he  called upon army to provide boats and  all helped us a lot so  so far as water was  water had the minimum level that boats  could play so now to send after  evacuation now our challenge is to reach  out to people who are still staying in  remote areas  rescue teams say despite high water  levels many villagers are unwilling to  leave those who have are hoping to  return soon so they can start rebuilding  their lives pav nimittal al-jazeera  hojai district in northeast india
 

